  "problem": "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2032}=2x-2y-3,\\,y(0)=1\n$$\n\nTo approximate the solution, one step of the Runge-Kutta method has already been computed, resulting in the following estimate:\n\n$$\ny(1)\u22480\n$$\n\nUse the $2$-Step Adams-Bashforth-Moulton Method with one step to approximate $y(2).$\n\n*Hint: The corrector equation of the two-step Adams-Bashforth-Moulton method is defined as*\n\n$$\n\u0394y=\\frac{1}{12}(5{y}_{p}^{\u2032}+8{y}^{\u2032}-{y}_{-1}^{\u2032})\\cdot \u0394x\n$$\n\n*where ${y}_{p}$ denotes the predictor at the current step, and ${y}_{-1}^{\u2032}$ is the estimated slope at the previous point.*",
